{"command": "cd /testbed && D=$(date +%F) && cat > .specify/memory/constitution.md <<EOF\n# cachetools Constitution\n<!-- Sync Impact Report (temporary scratch for review; remove before commit)\nVersion change: none (unfilled template) -> 1.0.0\nModified principles: none (all principles newly added)\nAdded principles:\n  I. Preserve Existing Public API Behavior\n  II. Testable Acceptance Criteria\n  III. Evidence Over Assertion\n  IV. Simple Scoped Implementations\n  V. Documented Assumptions and Regressions\nAdded sections: Scope and Deferred Intents; Development Workflow\nRemoved sections: none\nDeferred TODOs: none\n-->\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### I. Preserve Existing Public API Behavior\n\nAll changes MUST preserve the behavior of the existing public cachetools\nAPI: exposed names, signatures, documented semantics, and error behavior.\nNew features MUST be additive (for example, a new module such as\n`cachetools.tagged` built on the existing `LRUCache`) and MUST NOT alter,\nshadow, or remove existing behavior. Any intended change to an existing\npublic API MUST be recorded as a regression note and requires a\nconstitution amendment first.\n\nRationale: cachetools is a published library; downstream code depends on\nstable, predictable semantics.\n\n### II. Testable Acceptance Criteria\n\nEvery requirement MUST state observable, testable acceptance criteria\nbefore implementation starts. Each criterion MUST name the inputs, the\nexpected observable outcome (return value, raised exception, or state\nafter the operation), and any state-preservation guarantees (for example,\n\"rejecting invalid input MUST leave prior value, tags, and recency\nunchanged\"). A requirement that cannot be expressed as a failing-then-\npassing test MUST be rewritten or deferred, not implemented on\nassumption.\n\nRationale: testable criteria make completion verifiable and keep scope\nhonest.\n\n### III. Evidence Over Assertion\n\nClaims about behavior MUST distinguish observed evidence from unverified\nassertions. A behavior is \"verified\" only when a command was run and its\noutput shows the expected result; otherwise it MUST be labeled as an\nunverified assumption. Test evidence MUST cite the command and the\nobserved outcome (pass/fail counts or concrete output), never paraphrase\nwithout the underlying run.\n\nRationale: in an autonomous workflow, unmarked assumptions become silent\nregressions.\n\n### IV. Simple Scoped Implementations\n\nImplementations MUST be minimal and scoped to the stated requirement.\nPrefer the smallest change that satisfies the acceptance criteria; do not\nadd configuration, abstraction layers, or speculative features that the\ncriteria do not demand. Complexity MUST be justified against a specific\ncriterion, not anticipated need.\n\nRationale: small, scoped changes are easier to verify and less likely to\nviolate Principle I.\n\n### V. Documented Assumptions and Regressions\n\nUnresolved assumptions, open questions, and any behavior that regressed\nor was intentionally changed MUST be written down in project notes\n(HANDOFF.md or the feature spec) with the date and the evidence status\n(verified/unverified). Deferred candidate requirements (for example,\nclaim variants such as the 2026-09-21 put-recency extension) MUST be\ntracked as deferred intents, not silently dropped or silently adopted.\n\nRationale: later phases and reviewers need a complete, auditable record of\nwhat was assumed, what was deferred, and what changed.\n\n## Scope and Deferred Intents\n\nThe constitution governs process only; it does not authorize\nimplementation. The TaggedCache feature (R01-R03) and the Claim-A\ncandidate extension (put recency refresh, variant\nput_no_recency_refresh, 2026-09-21) are deferred to later Spec Kit phases\n(specify/plan/implement). Upstream tests MUST remain unchanged; project-\nowned tests and notes (for example HANDOFF.md) MAY be added.\n\n## Development Workflow\n\nWork proceeds through the Spec Kit phases (constitution, specify, plan,\nimplement, converge) with artifacts under `specs/` and\n`.specify/`. Each phase MUST close with a summary that cites the\nartifacts it produced and the commands it ran. Convergence MUST rerun\npublic acceptance (`acceptance_public.py`) and project tests and state\nany unresolved gaps explicitly.\n\n## Governance\n\nThis constitution supersedes conflicting local practices. Amendments MUST\nbe made by editing this file, bumping `Version` per semantic versioning\n(MAJOR: principle removed or redefined; MINOR: principle/section added or\nmaterially expanded; PATCH: wording/clarification), updating\n`Last Amended` to the ISO amendment date, and recording the change in a\nSync Impact Report for review. Compliance is reviewed at each phase\nclosing: evidence of compliance (test runs, preserved APIs, documented\nassumptions) MUST accompany the phase summary. Ratification date records\nthe original adoption and is not changed by amendments.\n\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Ratified**: $D | **Last Amended**: $D\nEOF\necho WROTE; grep -n \"CONSTITUTION_VERSION\\|PROJECT_NAME\\|PRINCIPLE_\" .specify/memory/constitution.md || echo NO_LEFTOVER_TOKENS; tail -3 .specify/memory/constitution.md", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "bash: line 1: cachetools.tagged: command not found\nbash: line 1: LRUCache: command not found\nbash: line 1: specs/: Is a directory\nbash: line 1: .specify/: Is a directory\nbash: line 1: acceptance_public.py: command not found\nbash: line 1: Version: command not found\nbash: line 1: Last: command not found\n", "stdout": "WROTE\nNO_LEFTOVER_TOKENS\nthe original adoption and is not changed by amendments.\n\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Ratified**: 2026-10-17 | **Last Amended**: 2026-10-17\n"}